# Runtime data — never build-context material, and dangerous if it ever is.
# These are empty in a fresh checkout, so they cost nothing today; the point is
# that a production host where uploads/ has grown, or where someone left a
# database dump next to the compose file, must not silently ship either into
# the builder stage.
apps/api/public/uploads
apps/api/logs
apps/api/storage

# Database dumps, ROOT LEVEL ONLY.
#
# Deliberately not `**/*.sql`: every Prisma migration is a file named
# migration.sql, the runner stage copies apps/api/prisma wholesale, and a
# recursive rule would ship migration directories that are empty. That breaks
# `prisma migrate deploy` in a way nothing warns about — the directory is
# present, the history table disagrees, and the failure surfaces later as drift.
#
# Docker matches with Go filepath.Match, where `*` does not cross `/`, so these
# already only bind at the context root. Keeping them un-starred documents the
# intent so a future edit does not "helpfully" make them recursive.
/*.sql
/*.sql.gz
/*.dump
/*.bak

# Agent/editor scratch
.claude
